el  of them the look of them everything now  here's the thing it's okay for this to  feel like a different movie marvel's got  their head around that Thor Iron Man  Captain  they're all sharing the same cinematic  universe but each of the individual  franchises feels fundamentally different  from the others that's how it should  have been with this and as I said Martin  Freeman really does bring this wonderful  lightness to the point that it's almost  like he's in a different movie but he's  the center even when his life's in  jeopardy you just get this feeling like  we're on a fun adventure and it's all  gonna be alright but then the minute the  focus goes off of him and we deal with  all of the dwarves over the politics go  out in lake town or we deal with the  oncoming necromancer suddenly it's not a  fun little venture that's all gonna be  alright now it's a building to war movie  it's not what the feel of the book was  and I want to be clear nine times out of  the ten you're better off changing it  for the movie I think if you make the  movie exactly as what was written in the  book there's no point but you have to  stay true to what the core of that  original source material was and they're  not doing that with these movies the  core of what these movies should have  been is in the heart of those moments  with Martin Freeman when he's fighting  the spiders on his own or even better  when he breaks through the the canopy  and Mirkwood when he's alone talking  with Smaug and trying to get the dragon  she's just keep talking so he can keep  himself alive can make you go haha this  is nice but these are fleeting moments  at best unexpected journey I was a  little annoyed this time  honestly I'm pissed off I incite this  whole thing was doomed to go this way  because they wanted to recapture Lord of  the Rings they didn't really want to  tell the story of The Hobbit if they  wanted to tell the story of The Hobbit  they wouldn't have been injecting all  this stuff t